  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Full-Stack Options**\n\nI\'m currently evaluating the potential for running either an Express backend with Vite or a full-stack server setup. I see the Vite configuration in `package.json` set to port 3000 and using `0.0.0.0` as the host. Now, I\'m trying to decide whether to integrate the two. I\'m focusing on the environmental constraints influencing this decision.\n\n\n**Refining Full-Stack Strategy**\n\nI\'ve decided to move forward with a full-stack approach, prioritizing a `server.ts` entry point using Express. During development, I\'ll mount `vite.middlewares` for integration. To launch the server, I\'ll use the command `\"start\": \"node server.ts\"`. I\'ve also just started updating `metadata.json` and `index.html`. I\'ve set the name to \"EduInclusiva - Sistema de PEI, PAEE e DUA 3.0\" with a description detailing its purpose and legal basis.\n\n\n"
