  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Network Issues**\n\nI\'ve been investigating the network behavior in the sandbox, particularly focusing on `generativelanguage.googleapis.com`. I\'ve observed that outbound requests are exhibiting intermittent issues such as hanging, failing, or timing out. Furthermore, there\'s a problem when the API is called from the browser in the preview iframe, with issues encountered when requesting `/api`.\n\n\n**Pinpointing the Root Cause**\n\nI\'ve homed in on the error\'s origin. The `/gemini/generate-pei` endpoint, or a similar GET request, seems to be failing, potentially due to a proxy issue. Consequently, the server returns HTML (`<!doctype html>`) instead of JSON, which is triggering a `SyntaxError` when the frontend attempts to parse it. This perfectly matches the error message: `error 0: SyntaxError: Unexpected token \'<\', \"<!doctype \"... is not valid JSON`. I\'m now auditing all instances of `fetch` and `JSON.parse` within the application, specifically in `src/components/AiGenerateModal.tsx`.\n\n\n"
