  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing NAPNE Data**\n\nI\'m now diving into the NAPNE data for the Para\303\255so campus. It appears I\'ve got some initial student count figures \342\200\223 29 students in total, and I see data for high school students as well. I\'ll need to explore how to extract more information from this.\n\n\n**Clarifying Para\303\255so Data**\n\nNow, I\'ve got a clearer picture for the Para\303\255so campus. It looks like the NAPNE data breaks down like this: 29 total students, 15 are in high school technical programs, while 14 are in higher education. I\'ve also verified that 24 students have confirmed diagnoses, including Autism Spectrum Disorder (Level 1 and 2), ADHD, Oppositional Defiant Disorder, and Giftedness.\n\n\n**Examining Student Cases**\n\nI\'m now assessing specific student cases. It seems I have a breakdown of student profiles including those with dual exceptionalities (like TEA/ADHD), learning disabilities (Dyslexia, Dyscalculia), physical/motor disabilities, visual and auditory impairments, and anxiety/mood disorders linked to neurodivergence. I\'ve also noted that five students are either without a formal diagnosis or are in the diagnostic investigation phase. I also see a critical legal point here, the absence of a medical report shouldn\'t hinder individualized educational plan (IEP) creation or NAPNE/AEE support. This is going to make the Para\303\255so campus stand out even more.\n\n\n"
