  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the User Input**\n\nI\'m now diving back into the user\'s attachment and prompt. The file name `estatisticas_napne_campus_paraiso_495545f4` suggests statistical data related to NAPNE at the Para\303\255so campus. I see the content includes a mention of Neurodivergences, and the quantity of students being followed. I\'ll need to decode this information and process it to figure out the user\'s request.\n\n\n**Interpreting the Data**\n\nI\'ve processed the numbers from the data. Specifically, I understand there are 29 students in total, split between high school (15) and college (14). Furthermore, I\'ve noted that 24 students have confirmed diagnoses, while 5 are suspected but not yet confirmed. I\'m now aligning these figures with the user\'s request to adapt to the campus conditions.\n\n\n**Clarifying Legal Frameworks**\n\nI\'m now integrating the legal and pedagogical foundation into the analysis. I\'m focusing on the implications of the MEC Portaria 421/2026, LBI (Law 13.146/2015), and PNEEI (Decree 12.686/2025). The key takeaway is that the PEI must be created regardless of diagnostic confirmation, prioritizing the removal of educational barriers and student strengths. I\'m considering how this informs the modifications needed for the Campus Para\303\255so version.\n\nI\'m synthesizing the core requirements for adapting the Ioda for Campus Para\303\255so. I\'ll need to update the institutional identification to \"NAPNE \302\267 Campus Para\303\255so\", and include the specific student data: 29 total, split between high school (15) and college (14), with 24 diagnosed and 5 suspected cases. This information helps structure our response.\n\n\n**Examining Student Profiles**\n\nI\'m now incorporating specific student profiles to enrich the analysis, including Lucas with Cerebral Palsy, Beatriz with low vision, and Matheus with ASD. I\'ve added a new profile: Larissa, who has both ADHD and High Abilities, offering insights on the need for a tailored approach. I\'m also including Cau\303\243, a student with no confirmed diagnosis but with a working hypothesis from the NAPNE.\n\n\n**Developing a Visual Dashboard**\n\nI\'m now designing the visual interface. I will create a \"Panorama NAPNE \302\267 Campus Para\303\255so\" display with key stats: 29 students total, 15 in high school, 14 in college, 24 confirmed diagnoses, and 5 with diagnostic hypotheses under investigation. I will also incorporate a legal compliance indicator, highlighting adherence to the MEC Portaria 421/2026. This data will be presented through banners, widgets or modals.\n\n\n"
