  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Student Data**\n\nI\'m currently focused on `StudentHeader.tsx`. I\'m exploring how to display specific badges based on the `status_diagnostico` field. If it\'s `\'confirmado\'`, I\'m considering an inline badge with a specific color and style, likely using Tailwind classes for efficiency.\n\n\n**Refining Status Display**\n\nI\'ve been refining the status badge display logic in `StudentHeader.tsx`. I\'m integrating specific styling for different diagnosis states. Confirmed diagnoses will get a green badge. Investigational hypotheses get amber. I\'m leveraging Tailwind for streamlined styling. I am also considering a collapsible banner with campus-wide NAPNE data.\n\n\n**Implementing New Modal Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating a new student addition modal, modifying `/components/AddStudentModal.tsx`. I\'ve added a \"Status Diagn\303\263stico\" selector with clear options and a helpful explanatory note based on MEC regulations. I\'m also including preset options for conditions specific to Campus Para\303\255so, aligning them with the provided list.\n\n\n"
