    thinking: "**Examining Initial Cases**\n\nI\'m currently reviewing the initial cases provided, specifically focusing on `initialCases.ts`. I\'ve started with `casoLucasTecnico`, involving Lucas Ferreira de Lima, a 17-year-old with a technical background and mild Cerebral Palsy. My next step is to examine the specifics of `casoBeatrizSuperior`.\n\n\n**Analyzing New Data**\n\nI\'ve expanded my analysis to include more student profiles. I am now looking at `casoBeatrizSuperior`, `casoMatheusMedio`, `casoLarissaSuperior`, and `casoSemLaudoHipotese`, all exported by `casosIniciais`. I am paying close attention to their technical skills and any relevant conditions like visual impairments, Autism Spectrum Disorder (ASD), and ADHD. The goal now is to see how these profiles align with creating a profile selector for the Ioda agent.\n\n\n**Designing User Experience**\n\nI am now focused on integrating real-world cases into the PEI generation process. I need to design the user experience in `AddStudentModal.tsx` and the backend in `server.ts` to make this work well. I want to build an intuitive, powerful, and authentic flow. This means considering the modal\'s design, especially the \"Institutional Profile Selector.\" I will look at presenting interactive cards/buttons for \"M\303\251dio T\303\251cnico em TI\" and \"Superior em TI\" profiles, and their subtitles, features, and student counts.\n\n\n**Implementing Profile Selector**\n\nI\'m currently working to implement the profile selector feature, focusing on the real-world cases from Campus Para\303\255so. I\'m visualizing the UI, envisioning buttons for \"Caso Lucas,\" \"Caso Matheus,\" and \"Caso Cau\303\243,\" to assist in making a profile selection. I am considering how the selection will automatically update the course, module, curricular component, and age, ensuring a seamless experience.\n\n\n**Defining Real-World Cases**\n\nI\'m now integrating the Campus Para\303\255so cases into the profile selector. Specifically, if \"Superior em TI\" is chosen, I am presenting real benchmarks: \"Caso Beatriz\" (low vision, SQL), \"Caso Larissa\" (ADHD, software engineering), and \"Caso Geral Superior\" (neurodivergence, system development). Each click pre-fills the form with high-quality real context from Campus Para\303\255so, while allowing teachers to freely edit any field. I will filter the \"Preencher por Condi\303\247\303\243o Mapeada\" based on the selected profile and add an informative callout from the Ioda Agent.\n\n\n**Incorporating DUA Principles**\n\nI\'m now integrating DUA 3.0 guidelines, focusing on real-world reference cases for the selected modality. In `server.ts`, specifically in `/api/gemini/generate-pei`, I\'m reading `perfilModalidade` and passing it to Gemini AI for use in the system and user prompts. If \'medio_tecnico\' is selected, the prompt will specify the student\'s enrollment in Ensino M\303\251dio T\303\251cnico Integrado em Inform\303\241tica, grounding the PEI on Campus Para\303\255so cases and highlighting specific supports. If it is \'superior_ti\', the prompt specifies the student\'s enrollment in Ensino Superior em TI (Sistemas de Informa\303\247\303\243o / Ci\303\252ncia da Computa\303\247\303\243o).\n\n\n"
