  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Accessibility Features**\n\nI\'m working on adding `AcessibilidadePreferencia` to `src/types/pei.ts`. Specifically, I\'ve defined `EscalaFonte` and `ModoContraste` types, which are integral to the `Preferencias` interface, reflecting preferred font sizes and contrast modes. I believe these additions will enhance the accessibility features.\n\n\n**Designing the Wizard**\n\nI\'m currently designing the progressive disclosure wizard for `AddStudentModal.tsx`, focusing on minimizing distractions and cognitive overload. I\'ve started structuring it as a stepper, with the first step dedicated to \"Perfil & Modalidade\". I\'ll be using icons for visual clarity, aiming for a streamlined and focused user experience. The goal is to keep the layout strictly centered on the pedagogical actions.\n\n\n**Structuring the Wizard Steps**\n\nI\'ve outlined the remaining steps for the progressive disclosure wizard. Step 2, \"Identifica\303\247\303\243o,\" will focus on basic student data and disciplines, marked by a `UserCheck` icon. Step 3, \"Estudo de Caso & DUA,\" is for barriers and assistive technologies, using a `Layers` icon. Finally, step 4, \"Revis\303\243o & Gera\303\247\303\243o Ioda\" will be for validation and AI, represented by `Sparkles`. I\'ve added a progress bar and clean step tabs with checkmarks to show completed steps. I am now working on step 1.\n\n\n**Mapping Student Cases**\n\nI\'m currently mapping real student cases to build out the \"Identifica\303\247\303\243o do Estudante\" step. I\'m focusing on scenarios like *Caso Cau\303\243*, and the related fields and logical flows. I\'m prioritizing diverse student profiles, including Beatriz\'s low vision case and Larissa\'s ADHD and high abilities. The progress also entails pre-filling data based on the chosen modality, such as the IT courses. I\'m also planning a banner clarifying that these cases are for pedagogical reference and data is customizable.\n\n\n**Developing Step 3**\n\nI\'m now implementing the \"Estudo de Caso & Barreiras\" step. I\'ve built the structure for a diagnostic situation card, allowing toggling between \"Diagn\303\263stico Confirmado\" and \"Sem Laudo\". The \"Sem Laudo\" option will display a legal guarantee card. I\'ve also designed a \"Solu\303\247\303\265es Prontas do Banco DUA 3.0\" card with a compact grid of solutions, automatically populating related fields upon selection.\n\n\n**Finalizing Step 4**\n\nI\'ve just added the \"Barreiras Observadas\" textarea with a DUA prompt and the \"Potencialidades e Tecnologias Assistivas\" card. This card has separate text areas for interests and assistive technologies. Now, the footer provides back navigation and the trigger for the AI generation. Step 4\'s review card summarizes student information, course, legal status, identified barriers, and suggested assistive technologies, acting as a final check before AI processing.\n\n\n**Implementing AI Generation**\n\nI\'ve incorporated the AI generation action box, featuring a callout explaining Ioda\'s function in synthesizing the PEI. A \"Gerar PEI Completo com Ioda AI\" primary button triggers the process, accompanied by a dynamic loading animation with three phases. A back-navigation button is included in the footer. I\'ve also implemented accessibility controls, integrating a persistent bar across pages for font size adjustments and contrast mode selection. This includes size selectors and contrast options tailored for varying visual needs.\n\n\n"
