    thinking: "**Prioritizing Privacy Safeguards**\n\nI\'m focused on removing personally identifiable information from the referenced case. It\'s a critical step, given privacy regulations. My priority is ensuring anonymity by eliminating student names and any data that could reveal their identities, like specific medical conditions, as the user instructed. The aim is to uphold the regulations, while keeping the other important relevant details.\n\n\n**Implementing Anonymization Measures**\n\nI\'m now implementing the anonymization changes, focusing on removing all personal data from the reference cases. Student names and sensitive information are being replaced with pedagogical codes, such as \"Estudante INF-01,\" as instructed, to comply with privacy regulations (LGPD and Decreto). I\'ve removed the buttons with student names in the `AddStudentModal.tsx` and now only present clean institutional options. This ensures data privacy while maintaining relevant context.\n\n\n**Designing New System Templates**\n\nI\'m developing generic technical templates for the system, inspired by the need for anonymized options. These include \"Modelo Padr\303\243o: Laborat\303\263rio de Programa\303\247\303\243o,\" \"Modelo Padr\303\243o: Redes e Infraestrutura,\" and others, all devoid of personal student data. My focus is on creating reusable, safe, and effective components, adhering to anonymization standards.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Adapting Typography and Structure**\n\nI\'m now changing the application\'s typography to reflect a modern style like iLovePDF, exploring Inter, Poppins, or Plus Jakarta Sans fonts with clean weights and tracking. The structural layout is being adapted to follow iLovePDF\'s model, using the provided screenshot as a guide. The color scheme will use either green and white or black and green for the app. The header will feature a logo inspired by iLovePDF.\n\n\n**Visualizing Interface Components**\n\nI\'m now visualizing the new user interface. I\'ve designed a top navigation bar with dropdowns and clean links for functions like \"Elaborar PEI\" and \"Estudo de Caso.\" There\'s also a user profile icon and quick accessibility buttons. The hero section will display a welcoming message and the platform\'s purpose. I\'m also implementing a pill filter bar, similar to iLovePDF\'s, to categorize content, and a card grid layout.\n\n\n**Defining Tool Card Layout**\n\nI\'m working on the design of the tool cards for the iLovePDF-style hub. Each card will have a subtle border and shadow that expands on hover. The top-left features a vibrant colored square icon. The card\'s content includes a bold title, like \"Novo PEI Inteligente (Ioda AI)\", and a concise two-line description, such as \"Criar um novo Plano de Ensino Individualizado via assistente passo a passo com DUA 3.0.\" I\'m also planning the specific tools to include in the hub.\n\n\n**Listing Hub Tools**\n\nNow I\'m listing the specific tools for the hub, as the user requested. These will include a standardized IFTO/MEC form with eight editable sections for printing/exporting. There is a bank of DUA 3.0 solutions for IT lab accommodations, SMART goals management, and also guidelines for students with a diagnostic hypothesis but no formal diagnosis. Plus, a campus census and statistics panel, and a print/export function are planned, too.\n\n\n**Refining Navigation Design**\n\nI\'m now refining the navigation options to ensure easy transitions. The goal is a clean view with a \"\342\206\220 Voltar ao Hub de Ferramentas\" button, or tabs in the header allowing switching between Hub and views. I\'m prioritizing user flow and ease of access to tools and content. I need to make sure that the layout of the UI complies with the instructions given. I\'ll need to do some more work to ensure the designs follow the specifications from the iLovePDF model.\n\n\n**Creating Template Definitions**\n\nI\'ve just defined new, anonymous templates: \"Template A: Laborat\303\263rio de Programa\303\247\303\243o & L\303\263gica,\" \"Template B: Redes de Computadores & Hardware,\" \"Template C: Banco de Dados Relacional & SQL,\" and \"Template D: Acompanhamento Pedag\303\263gico Inicial.\" These templates are compliant with LGPD. I\'m also ensuring a clean, modern font setup using Inter or a similar sans-serif for improved readability. The structural and visual style will follow the iLovePDF model.\n\n\n"
