  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Anonymizing Student Data**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `src/data/initialCases.ts` file, ensuring strict LGPD compliance regarding student data. My approach involves anonymizing student names to prevent privacy breaches. I\'m starting by renaming student-specific identifiers like `casoLucasTecnico` to something more generic, such as `casoEstudanteInf01`.\n\n\n**Refining Data Anonymization**\n\nI\'ve continued the data scrubbing in `src/data/initialCases.ts`, updating student identifiers and names.  I\'ve replaced further specific case names with generic labels and adjusted student names to reflect these new, anonymous identifiers. Export alias variables are now deemed unnecessary; updating exports seems cleaner. Next, I\'ll analyze the visual structure to apply analogous design choices to the `I\360\237\222\232PEI` app.\n\n\n**Designing the Feature Cards**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing the feature cards for the interface, drawing inspiration from iLovePDF\'s layout. I envision a clean, white card design with rounded corners, responsive grid layout, and a colored square icon in the upper left. I\'m aiming for a visual structure that is intuitive and engaging, ensuring that the design is responsive and user-friendly across all devices. The cards will present titles in bold and concise descriptions. I want them to have hover effects to indicate interactivity.\n\n\n**Integrating Detailed Views**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the user flow after a card is selected. My current thinking revolves around integrating detailed views and modal actions seamlessly. I\'ve considered that when a card is clicked, modals will open for certain actions, while other cards will trigger a smooth navigation to a dedicated view. I aim to ensure a clear \"Return to Hub\" button. I\'m also planning a prominent student selection bar.\n\n\n"
