  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Student Data**\n\nI\'m currently focused on processing student data across various cases, including those labeled as `casoLucasTecnico`, `casoBeatrizSuperior`, `casoMatheusRedes`, `casoLarissaSuperior`, and `casoCauaSemLaudo`. My immediate task involves anonymizing the header and observation texts for privacy, starting with \'Estudante INF-0\'. This is to ensure secure data handling before further analysis.\n\n\n**Identifying Student Characteristics**\n\nI\'ve moved on to examining student profiles beyond simple case labeling, now looking into individual characteristics and the context of their work. I am noting details like the level of study (Technical or Superior), and specifics extracted from `observacoes_docente`, `painel_notas`, and `parecer_pedagogico` for each student. I am analyzing the content to understand how they are being evaluated.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Data Privacy**\n\nI\'ve shifted focus to data privacy concerns, specifically addressing the reference case block in Step 1. I\'m removing the cases that include student names and conditions to ensure privacy. Instead, I\'m integrating neutral pedagogical templates like \"Laborat\303\263rio de Programa\303\247\303\243o\" and \"Redes e Infraestrutura,\" or simplifying the flow to select the modality.\n\n\n**Designing the Layout**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing the iLovePDF-inspired design. I\'m taking the visual cues from the layout requirements and image. I\'m paying particular attention to the top header elements, including the `i\360\237\222\232PEI` logo (using the same structure as `i\360\237\222\232PDF`), the navigation options (`IN\303\215CIO / HUB`, etc.), and the user avatar with accessibility features. I\'m also planning the hero section content with the introductory message.\n\n\n**Structuring the User Interface**\n\nI\'m now diving into the user interface components. I am planning the layout, including a subtitle for the platform, an active student banner with a selector, and a filter pills bar mirroring iLovePDF\'s design. I\'m focusing on the grid of tool cards, considering column arrangements for various screen sizes, icon styles, and text descriptions to ensure usability.\n\n\n**Developing Tool Cards**\n\nI\'m presently focused on the tool card design. I\'ve defined styles for regular and hover states, including a slight lift effect and shadow on hover. I\'m incorporating the four specific cards: \"Novo PEI com Ioda AI,\" \"Plano de Ensino (PEI),\" \"Estudo de Caso & Barreiras,\" and \"Modelo Oficial NAPNE / MEC.\" Each will have a distinct icon and concise description of its functionality. I will ensure a consistent and user-friendly visual experience.\n\n\n**Expanding Tool Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating new functionalities into the tool cards. I am focusing on the \"Banco de Solu\303\247\303\265es DUA 3.0\" which will offer a catalog of assistive technologies. I\'m also adding a \"Painel de Acompanhamento\" with features for monitoring SMART goals and student autonomy, which are designed to support and improve learning experiences. I am also adding a card to guide on the legal aspects for students with an unconfirmed diagnosis, based on Portaria MEC 421/2026. Lastly, a new tool for generating statistics from the campus census will be included. A print and save to PDF feature will complete the card features.\n\n\n**Implementing Navigation Flow**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the user navigation. The design ensures that when the user is in the `hub` tab (`activeTab === \'hub\'`), they see the iLovePDF-style hub with the tool cards. Clicking any card takes them to the detailed view. Within each detailed view, there is a \"\342\206\220 Voltar ao In\303\255cio (Hub de Ferramentas)\" button, and the Student Switcher. Also, in the Navbar, clicking the logo `i\360\237\222\232PEI` or `Hub de Ferramentas` always redirects to the Hub!\n\n\n"
