  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Home Page Focus**\n\nI\'m digging deeper into the user\'s feedback. They\'re clearly advocating for a streamlined home page, prioritizing the \"PEI\" focus. My analysis suggests condensing less crucial tools like warranty, census, and solutions bank to a consolidated, accessible location. This home page will show the bare essentials.\n\n\n**Prioritizing PEI Essentials**\n\nI\'ve finalized the essential \"cards\" for the home page, focusing exclusively on the PEI workflow. I\'ve curated the six core functions: creation, management, case study, formal document, monitoring, and export. The warranty, census, and solutions bank will now reside in a dedicated support and settings menu, streamlining the user experience and decluttering the initial interface.\n\n\n**Integrating Support and Privacy**\n\nI\'m now incorporating user preferences regarding support resources and student privacy. I\'m placing the warranty, census, and solutions bank, as well as new support options in a discreet dropdown. Furthermore, I\'ve clarified the student name display logic; the name should only appear within a specific PEI context, not on the general home or hub pages, maintaining confidentiality.\n\n\n**Revising Student Context**\n\nI\'m now revising the student context on the home and hub pages. I agree, showing a specific student\'s PEI details directly on these pages is unnecessary. I\'m replacing this with a general template, overview or guide, perhaps titled \"Guia de Elabora\303\247\303\243o do PEI,\" with suggestions and guidelines for PEI creation, accompanied by a clear selector to open or create a new PEI. I am also planning to ensure that there is no student name in the banner of the hub page.\n\n\n**Clarifying Student Display**\n\nI\'ve got the student name display logic figured out. Outside of the specific PEI view, I\'ll use anonymized identifiers like \"Estudante 01 - T\303\251cnico em Inform\303\241tica\" or an anonymized code (\"INF-01 \302\267 2\302\272 Ano\") in the selector. However, the student\'s full name will proudly appear within the PEI document itself (when the user clicks into it, e.g. Estudo de Caso). I\'ll keep both the full name and anonymized code in `initialCases.ts`. I also simplified the hub, focusing on PEI operations, removing the clutter.\n\n\n"
