  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Privacy Concerns**\n\nI understand the need to balance transparency with student privacy. I\'m thinking about how to present student names within PEIs while respecting confidentiality. Showing examples or templates of PEIs, especially those integrated into the tool hub, feels like a good way to demonstrate the format without compromising individual privacy. I\'m focusing on ensuring the information is accessible but anonymized where needed.\n\n\n**Refining PEI Display**\n\nI\'ve clarified how to handle student names in PEIs. When outside specific PEI access, I\'ll use institutional codes or placeholders for confidentiality. Within the Hub, I\'ll offer a guide and template of what a PEI is and how to build one. There will be a list or card interface to select a specific student\'s PEI, and inside that, the student\'s full name will be shown.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Core Features**\n\nI am now focusing on streamlining the home page. I\'m removing extraneous tools, leaving only what\'s directly essential for PEI creation and management. Additional features, such as the guarantee, census, and solution bank, will be housed within a separate configuration or support menu accessible from the hub, keeping the core experience clean and focused.\n\n\n**Developing PEI Structure**\n\nI\'m now structuring the PEI creation process as a step-by-step assistant with goals and DUA 3.0. I\'m focusing on curriculum access, methodological flexibility, and learning goals within the PEI, including case studies, accessibility, the official IFTO document format, and continuous student development tracking. I will also make the documents exportable in PDF or for official printing. The menu is being reorganized to prioritize the PEI tools.\n\n\n"
