  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Privacy Requirements**\n\nI\'ve been examining the student names in `initialCases.ts` and the user\'s specific request for the PEI context. The goal is to balance presenting student names with respecting their privacy, especially outside of the PEI context. I am now trying to formulate a clear rule for displaying names or anonymizing them based on where they appear, keeping privacy the focus.\n\n\n**Clarifying Display Rules**\n\nI\'ve refined my thinking on displaying student names. The core principle remains privacy. Inside a specific PEI, the student\'s name should be visible. Outside of that context \342\200\223 in the tool hub, public cards, or navigation \342\200\223 I\'ll ensure the student names are anonymized, using labels like \"PEI #01 - T\303\251cnico Integrado\" to maintain privacy.\n\n\n**Refining Presentation Options**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how student data is presented in different contexts. My new strategy prioritizes anonymity in the tool hub, especially on that active student card in `ILovePeiHub.tsx`. I think a template or suggestion card is better there, instead of showing a specific student. I have come to the conclusion that names are ONLY necessary in the PEI itself.\n\n\n**Developing PEI Structure**\n\nI\'m now thinking about how to improve the hub for creating and accessing PEIs. I\'m leaning toward an interactive PEI template guide, explaining all eight blocks, with actionable suggestions. I\'m also planning a quick-access selector so teachers can open a student\'s PEI, revealing the student\'s name only within that specific document.\n\n\n**Simplifying Hub Experience**\n\nI\'m now streamlining the Home page (Hub) for a better user experience. My current plan is to keep only the core PEI-focused cards on the main view. I intend to tuck away less-frequently used tools, such as the census, solution bank, and quality assurance, in a dedicated \"Configuration\" or \"Support\" menu, making them accessible but not cluttering the primary interface.\n\n\n"
