  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Privacy Considerations**\n\nOkay, I\'m now delving into the privacy implications, specifically concerning student names within PEI objects. I\'ve pinpointed that the name should be included within the objects themselves, but kept confidential in external presentations. This aims to balance data usability with student privacy concerns, a key challenge in this part of the design.\n\n\n**Refining Data Display**\n\nI\'ve just refined how student data will be displayed. Inside the PEI objects, full names like Lucas Ferreira de Lima are included, alongside institutional codes. However, outside the PEI, in the hub or switcher, names are replaced. Instead, I show details like \"PEI #01 \302\267 T\303\251cnico em Inform\303\241tica (2\302\272 Ano)\" or codes like \"INF-01\". This approach aims to provide necessary context while preserving student anonymity in broader interfaces.\n\n\n**Adjusting PEI Displays**\n\nI\'m now changing how the PEI is displayed for the teacher. When they open a specific PEI, the student\'s full name will be shown in the `PeiView`, `CaseStudyView`, `OfficialTemplateView`, `PeiPainelView`, `StudentHeader`, and Print view components. However, I\'ve removed the specific student card from the top banner of the hub, in `ILovePeiHub.tsx`. Instead, I\'ll render the \"Template Oficial do PEI & Guia de Estrutura\303\247\303\243o\" with the 8 official blocks and drafting suggestions.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Core Features**\n\nI\'m now focusing on simplifying the interface. I believe that the home page should only show the essential elements, namely, a clean action card or list titled \"**Meus PEIs Cadastrados (Acesso Confidencial)**\", displaying available PEIs by course and year without revealing personal names. A button to open each PEI, revealing the student\'s name only when selected, will be included, as well as a prominent button to \"Elaborar Novo PEI com Ioda AI.\" I\'ll move secondary features like guarantees, censuses, and solution banks to a secondary menu for easy access.\n\n\n**Simplifying Homepage Layout**\n\nI\'m now streamlining the homepage. The primary focus is now the PEI creation and management process. I\'m reducing the tools grid to only contain core PEI-related operations: creating a new PEI with Ioda AI, accessing existing PEIs, exploring case studies, accessing the official PEI model, tracking progress, and exporting PEIs. Less essential options like \"Garantia Sem Laudo\", \"Censo Campus\", and \"Banco de Solu\303\247\303\265es DUA\" are removed from the main grid. They will be accessible via a \"Suporte & Diretrizes\" dropdown menu in the top navigation bar.\n\n\n"
