  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Page Focus**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into `ILovePeiHub.tsx`, specifically focusing on the user\'s feedback. I realize I\'ve included too many tools on the home page, which is distracting from the core focus on the PEI. My goal now is to streamline the home page to include only essential elements, while consolidating less critical tools like warranties, census data, and the solution bank into a dedicated, accessible location.\n\n\n**Revising Student Data Access**\n\nI\'m working on how student names are displayed within the PEI framework. I want to ensure privacy by only showing a specific student\'s name once their PEI is accessed directly. The sidebar PEI hub, however, should showcase a generic template or structure, avoiding individual student identification. The updated ILovePeiHub.tsx focuses on displaying the template and guidance.\n\n\n**Structuring PEI Templates**\n\nI am now focusing on restructuring the PEI templates for optimal accessibility and adherence to guidelines. Specifically, I\'m integrating elements for Engagement, Representation, and Action/Expression, aligning with DUA 3.0 principles. I am also working on a \"R\303\251gua de Coer\303\252ncia Curricular\" to maintain core curriculum competence. A new \"+ Elaborar Novo PEI com Ioda AI\" button will be the primary call-to-action. I\'m exploring how to best organize and display existing PEIs using institutional codes to ensure external privacy.\n\n\n\n**Organizing Home Page Display**\n\nI\'m now streamlining the home page display. The system will select a specific student upon clicking \"Open PEI,\" directly accessing the PEI view with their full name and official information displayed. The home page will now include only six essential PEI cards focusing on core functionalities: Creating a new PEI with Ioda AI, curriculum plans and SMART goals, case studies and barriers, the official IFTO PEI template, progress and evaluation, and export/print options.\n\n\n"
