  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 3
    session_summary: "<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - **User Request**: Fix the error in the application: `error 0: Gemini API call timed out or hit quota; utilizing Ioda Pedagogical Engine: {\"error\":{\"code\":429,\"message\":\"You exceeded your current quota, please check your plan and billing details...\",\"status\":\"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\"}}`.\n   - **Core Deliverable**: Ensure that when the Gemini API returns a 429 quota error or times out during PEI generation / assistance, the application handles it gracefully without throwing an unhandled error or showing a broken UI. The fallback (Ioda Pedagogical Engine / local rule-based heuristic generator) should take over seamlessly, provide immediate high-quality PEI drafts according to the IFTO / MEC 421/2026 / DUA 3.0 standards, and inform the user calmly with a friendly status indicator rather than a raw API failure/crash.\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - Investigated `/src` structure: contains `App.tsx`, `components/`, `data/`, `index.css`, `main.tsx`, `types/`.\n   - In previous turns:\n     - Updated student names (`Lucas Ferreira de Lima`, `Beatriz Santos Rocha`, `Matheus Alencar da Silva`, `Larissa Menezes Costa`, `Cau\303\243 Ribeiro dos Santos`) inside their respective PEI objects in `src/data/initialCases.ts`.\n     - Created `getIdentificadorConfidencial` in `src/data/initialCases.ts` so student names are kept confidential outside the PEI (Hub / selectors) and only revealed when opening the specific PEI.\n     - Streamlined `ILovePeiHub.tsx` to 6 essential tools, added the 8-block official PEI template visual guide, and added practical suggestions for PEI elaboration.\n     - Unified support resources (Banco DUA, Censo Campus, Garantia sem Laudo MEC 421/2026) in a `Suporte & Diretrizes` dropdown menu in `Navbar.tsx`.\n     - Verified build (`compile_applet`) and lint (`lint_applet`) both passed cleanly.\n\n3. **Key Findings**\n   - The error log specifies: `Gemini API call timed out or hit quota; utilizing Ioda Pedagogical Engine: {\"error\":{\"code\":429,...}}`.\n   - Need to inspect where Gemini API calls are made: check `src/components/AddStudentModal.tsx`, `src/services/` or wherever Gemini generation logic is implemented.\n   - Per Gemini API guidelines: client should use `@google/genai` or standard fetch proxy, but when rate-limited (HTTP 429 / RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED) or offline, the local pedagogical engine must seamlessly synthesize the 8-block PEI response using the domain data (DUA 3.0, IFTO template, Portaria MEC 421/2026) without breaking UI execution or throwing uncaught console errors.\n\n4. **Errors & Fixes**\n   - **Error 0**: `Gemini API call timed out or hit quota; utilizing Ioda Pedagogical Engine: {\"error\":{\"code\":429,\"message\":\"You exceeded your current quota...\",\"status\":\"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\"}}`.\n   - Root cause: External Gemini API free quota limit reached (HTTP 429). The app logged or surfaced the raw 429 quota exhaustion.\n   - Fix to implement: Ensure the catch block catches 429 / quota exhaustion cleanly, activates the built-in deterministic pedagogical engine silently or with an informative notice (\"Modo Offline / Motor Pedag\303\263gico Ioda Ativo\"), and generates the complete, rich 8-block PEI directly from case data.\n\n5. **Active Context**\n   - App URL: `https://ais-dev-krwzzynhegkqukx43cumqj-729395395096.us-west2.run.app`\n   - Dev server running on port 3000.\n   - Codebase is TypeScript + React + Tailwind CSS on Vite.\n\n6. **Next Steps**\n   - Step 1: Search for where `fetch`, `Gemini`, `generateContent`, or `Ioda Pedagogical Engine` is defined (likely in `src/components/AddStudentModal.tsx` or `src/services/`).\n   - Step 2: Examine the Gemini calling logic and error-handling mechanism.\n   - Step 3: Implement robust error handling:\n     - Wrap API call with timeout and quota check (`err.status === 429 || err?.message?.includes(\'429\') || err?.message?.includes(\'quota\')`).\n     - Suppress raw console error explosion, smoothly fall back to the built-in Ioda Pedagogical Engine.\n     - Add user-friendly badge/toast in the UI: *\"Motor Pedag\303\263gico Ioda (Modo Local/Resiliente Ativo)\"* so the user gets an instant, perfectly structured PEI even with quota limitations.\n   - Step 4: Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` to verify compilation.\n\n7. **Commitments & Constraints**\n   - Do not display raw API keys or error stack traces to user.\n   - Maintain the strict 8-block IFTO structure, DUA 3.0 principles (CAST 2024), and Portaria MEC n\302\272 421/2026 guidelines.\n   - Preserve student confidentiality outside the PEI and full real name visibility inside the PEI.\n</summary>"
