    thinking: "**Investigating Timeout Behavior**\n\nI\'m now diving into `src/components/AddStudentModal.tsx`, specifically lines 355-357. I\'m focusing on the `catch` block where the application generates via the Ioda Pedagogical Engine due to a timeout. The `console.warn` is especially interesting. I need to understand why this timeout is happening, how often, and if it is impacting the user experience.\n\n\n**Analyzing Error Messaging**\n\nI\'ve realized the `console.warn` message in `AddStudentModal.tsx` handles both fetch failures and timeouts. Digging deeper, I found the client-side log, which includes the `genError.message` from the server. The timeout issue originates in `server.ts` where a Gemini API call is being handled. This message is sent to `process.stderr`. This should clarify why the timeout is happening and where the notice is coming from.\n\n\n**Improving Error Handling**\n\nI\'m now focusing on improving the error handling within `server.ts` to make it more resilient. I\'ve identified that quota limits and timeouts from the Gemini API are currently causing issues. I\'m considering implementing a cooldown period or caching strategy for the API key to prevent repeated 429 errors. I\'m also planning to change the logging from `console.warn` (which goes to stderr) to `console.log` (which goes to stdout) for these specific error scenarios, ensuring better log management. I\'m checking if `synthesizeIodaPei` is complete.\n\n\n"
