    thinking: "**Analyzing the Request**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the user\'s request. It seems they want me to update something related to \"Barreiras e DUA\" for a \"etapa 3,\" specifically concerning neurodivergences. The specific neurodivergences mentioned are ADHD and, well, I need to continue parsing the request to determine what \"Transtorno do Espect\" refers to. I\'m focusing on the implied task: listing and updating a given set of neurodivergences in this context.\n\n\n**Identifying Neurodivergences**\n\nI\'ve expanded my understanding of the neurodivergences involved. Now, my focus is on precisely identifying the specific conditions to be addressed. I\'m noting the inclusion of Autism Spectrum Disorder (TEA), anxiety disorders, specific learning disorders (dyslexia, dysgraphia, dyscalculia), intellectual disability, OCD, mixed anxiety-depressive disorder, depressive disorders, and epilepsy/seizures. I\'m also reviewing the provided documents to gather further context.\n\n\n**Mapping the Infrastructure**\n\nI\'m now mapping the available resources and curriculum. I\'m focusing on the computer labs: TO (Robotics and AI), LADES (Development), and LABIN (Library and Residence), noting the number and specifications of the PCs. Section 2.3.10 emphasizes accessibility across several areas. I\'m also reviewing the curriculum, particularly the first three periods, to see where the topic might fit in.\n\n\n**Reviewing the Curriculum**\n\nMy attention is now on the curriculum details. I\'m carefully reviewing course outlines for specific integration points. The focus is now the course structure, specifically the subjects listed in the 6th, 7th, and 8th periods: Artificial Intelligence, IT Management, and Project Management in IT, are of immediate interest. I\'m also now analyzing the syllabus for Software Engineering II for 2026/2.\n\n\n**Evaluating Software Quality**\n\nI\'m now delving into software quality standards and methodologies. I\'m looking at models for software process improvement, quality assurance techniques, and the concepts and applications of software testing, especially in the quality context. I\'m focusing on Test-Driven Development (TDD), test automation, test case generation, and relevant testing tools. I am also considering test plans, test process management, and issue tracking using tools like Jira and Bugzilla. I am paying close attention to quality standards (ISO/IEC 25010, ISO/IEC/IEEE 12207, CMMI, MPS.BR).\n\n\n**Refining Categorization**\n\nI\'m now refining the categorization of neurodivergences, paying close attention to both neurodivergent and physical/sensory conditions. I\'m focusing on how these conditions manifest as specific barriers within the lab setting and curriculum, and how best to represent them in an interactive user interface within `AddStudentModal.tsx`. I\'m focused on clear labeling and categorization to enhance user understanding. The goal is to highlight relevant course content and potential challenges, specifically targeting the undergraduate Systems Analysis and Development program (and technical secondary program in Informatics) at IFTO Campus Para\303\255so, with examples in subjects like Software Engineering II, Algorithms, and Databases.\n\n\n"
