  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Prompt\'s Core**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the user\'s request. I\'m focusing on the specific neurodivergences mentioned and how they relate to \"para a etapara 3 Barreiras e DUA\". My goal is to understand the precise context and intended output format before proceeding with a detailed analysis. I\'m prioritizing clarity about the request\'s core components.\n\n\n**Defining the Key Categories**\n\nI\'ve identified the specific conditions the user wants me to address: anxiety disorders, specific learning disorders, intellectual disability, OCD, and depressive disorders, alongside epilepsy and seizures. The user\'s request involves incorporating these conditions into \"para a etapara 3 Barreiras e DUA\", referencing attached course materials. I\'m starting to understand how to categorize and structure the output around these identified categories and materials.\n\n\n**Categorizing Further Conditions**\n\nI\'m now integrating \"transtornos depressivos,\" and \"epilepsia e crises convulsivas\" into the existing framework. I\'m carefully considering how to incorporate these new elements alongside the previously identified anxieties, learning disorders, intellectual disability, and OCD. I\'m also starting to analyze the provided course documents to define the context for incorporating these conditions.\n\n\n**Mapping the Educational Context**\n\nI\'m now diving into the course specifics to frame the neurodivergence considerations effectively. I\'m focusing on the Software Quality course in the first trimester, the Test of Software course in the second trimester, and all other courses specified in the program. This information helps me connect the neurodivergence categories to concrete learning scenarios, enabling the user to apply these concepts in a practical setting. I\'m ensuring I\'m mapping these topics.\n\n\n**Defining User\'s Preferences**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the user\'s preference for the output format. I\'m extracting key elements, specifically tailoring: the observed condition and related barriers, the potential interests, and adaptive technologies and flexibilities (DUA 3.0), all within the context of IFTO Campus Para\303\255so\'s labs and activities. Also, I\'m working to connect specific course contexts, allowing for a choice or auto-completion of courses and relevant course disciplines.\n\n\n**Updating Pedagogical Strategies**\n\nI am now focusing on integrating the nine specified neurodivergences, including ADHD, into the \"bancoDeSolucoesPedagogicas\" data structure. I\'m building detailed profiles based on the PPC and Plano de Ensino to refine pedagogical approaches, particularly highlighting DUA 3.0 content. For ADHD, I\'m specifically addressing barriers like difficulty sustaining attention, focusing on engagement through agile methods, and representing information with checklists and code models.\n\n\n**Integrating TEA into Scope**\n\nI\'m now incorporating specific strategies for students with Autism Spectrum Disorder (ASD). I\'m focusing on \"DUA A\303\247\303\243o e Express\303\243o\" by suggesting partial delivery of unit tests using a TDD cycle, summarized Markdown documentation, and extended time (+50%). I\'m also considering resources like Kanban boards in Jira, VS Code focus extensions, Pomodoro timers, and noise-canceling headphones to address barriers such as sensory overload, routine disruptions, and ambiguous instructions. The focus is on providing predictability through weekly schedules and structured testing routines. I\'m focusing on step-by-step checklists and test cases presented in tables, specifying expected inputs and outputs.\n\n\n**Refining Support Strategies**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on integrating support strategies for anxiety disorders. I\'m focusing on \"DUA A\303\247\303\243o e Express\303\243o,\" suggesting options like group presentations or recorded videos to alleviate cognitive blocks. I\'m considering using rubrics and lab guides in the Moodle environment to reduce evaluation pressure. I\'m also planning accommodations like extended time (+50%) for demonstrations, or the option of individualized technical defenses with recordings. Furthermore, I\'m integrating noise-canceling headphones (27dB), sensory pause cards, Markdown guides and automated test suites.\n\n\n\n**Adapting Anxiety Solutions**\n\nI\'m now honing strategies for anxiety related to deadlines. I\'m focusing on \"DUA A\303\247\303\243o e Express\303\243o\", by suggesting extended time (+50%) for coding projects and tests, along with emotional regulation breaks (5-10 minutes). Additionally, I\'m proposing segmented evaluations. I\'m considering assistive technologies such as IDE autocompletion extensions, detailed evaluation rubrics, and personalized support for individual presentations with the instructor.\n\n\n\n**Incorporating TA Resources**\n\nI\'m now integrating assistive technologies (TA) to enhance accessibility. I am focusing on DUA Action and Expression by using modern IDEs with visual linters in real time, along with text-to-speech for reading instructions, extended time (+50%) for defense of the algorithmic solution, and an oral presentation. I\'m also including TA resources such as OpenDyslexic or JetBrains Mono fonts, visual linters (Error Lens, Prettier), text-to-speech reader for both the screen and PDFs in Portuguese, a calculator and permitted reference tables.\n\n\n**Refining OCD Strategies**\n\nI\'m now focusing on OCD-specific interventions, specifically addressing cognitive rigidity and perfectionism. I\'m leveraging the \"DUA Engajamento\" principle to establish clear \"Definition of Done\" criteria and setting refactoring limits to avoid counterproductive loops. I will also incorporate simplified development interfaces, step-by-step illustrated guides, and pedagogical support from NAPNE. The output will facilitate a practical assessment centered on executing specific tasks, such as running automated tests and guided troubleshooting, alongside extended time (+100%) and mediated assistance from a monitor.\n\n\n**Integrating Mixed Conditions**\n\nI\'m now incorporating strategies for mixed anxiety and depressive disorders, focusing on DUA Engagement. I\'m prioritizing providing a secure pedagogical environment with clear, achievable goals. I\'m also planning for flexibility in deadlines, and incorporating assistive technologies to give objective feedback, such as automated test pipelines and bug tracking tools. My focus is on addressing energy fluctuations and performance anxieties.\n\n\n**Structuring Depression Interventions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on depressive disorders, specifically addressing cognitive slowing and fatigue. I\'m leveraging DUA Engagement by incorporating pair programming for collaborative support and short-term goal setting. Also, I\'m integrating DUA Representation, making recorded lectures and lab guides accessible via Moodle. I\'m also considering DUA Action and Expression through a flexible activity structure.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Safety Measures**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating support for epilepsy and seizure disorders, specifically concerning safety protocols. I\'m focusing on incorporating these interventions into the framework. This includes ensuring a calm lab environment, prioritizing clear visual representation and providing appropriate screen setups to prevent triggers. I\'m also planning for scheduled breaks and aligning health protocols with campus health services. The priority is to provide an accessible and safe learning experience.\n\n\n**Expanding Safety Protocols**\n\nI\'m now integrating safety protocols for epilepsy and seizure disorders. I\'ll ensure 45-minute screen breaks, extended assessment time (+50%), and the option to reschedule evaluations after a crisis. For assistive technology, I\'ll include blue light filters, adjusted monitor refresh rates, permitted special glasses, and accessible seating. This complements existing solutions for visual, auditory, and physical impairments. I\'ve also identified the data structure for solutions (`bancoDeSolucoesPedagogicas`) in `src/data/initialCases.ts` and in `src/components/AddStudentModal.tsx`, step 3, which must present nine neurodivergences as interactive elements.\n\n\n"
