    thinking: "**Analyzing the Query Details**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the user\'s specific request. I\'m focusing on the terms \"etapa 3 Barreiras e DUA\" and the neurodivergences mentioned: TDAH and TEA. My goal is to determine the context and the precise information needed for the update. I need to understand the intent behind the request, in order to respond properly.\n\n\n**Expanding the Scope**\n\nI\'ve broadened the scope to incorporate additional neurodivergences and conditions beyond the initial request. I\'m now considering anxiety disorders (generalized, phobic, panic, etc.), specific learning disorders (dyslexia, dysgraphia, dyscalculia), intellectual disability, obsessive-compulsive disorder (OCD), mixed anxiety and depressive disorder, depressive disorders, and epilepsy/seizures. I\'m also planning to utilize the course curriculum file.\n\n\n**Incorporating Relevant Details**\n\nI\'m now integrating information about depressive disorders and epilepsy into my analysis, alongside the course profile details. I\'m focusing on how these conditions might intersect with the course curriculum, particularly software engineering principles and testing methodologies. The course profile is very helpful, as I consider the lab spaces and relevant courses. I will now integrate the curriculum into the overall thought process.\n\n\n**Defining Preset Options**\n\nI\'m now focused on the content and functionality of `AddStudentModal.tsx`, specifically steps 1 and 2. I\'m prioritizing the inclusion of preset buttons or selections for courses and subjects drawn from the PPC and Plano de Ensino documents. I\'ve designed several presets covering a range of courses, like Systems, and subjects, like Software Engineering and Algorithms. This simplifies the course profile definition, grounding it in the official documents.\n\n\n**Structuring the Selector**\n\nI\'m now focused on Step 3, \"Etapa 3: Estudo de Caso, Barreiras & DUA.\" I\'m organizing the interface elements, specifically a clear selector for the nine neurodivergences. Each selection will highlight and auto-populate the necessary text areas for \"Barreiras Observadas,\" \"Estrat\303\251gias DUA,\" and \"Resultados Esperados.\" I want to make the structure visually appealing and easy to use.\n\n\n**Refining Data Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the final pieces, specifically focusing on data structures and backend logic. I\'m updating `bancoDeSolucoesPedagogicas` in `initialCases.ts` to ensure all nine neurodivergences are fully represented with comprehensive DUA 3.0 remedies tailored to IT courses like Software Engineering II. I\'m also preparing to update `server.ts` so `synthesizeIodaPei` correctly processes each neurodivergence and incorporates the curriculum when generating the PEI. Finally, I will integrate the available features within the Lab context.\n\n\n"
