  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Expanding Pedagogical Solutions**\n\nI\'m currently focused on expanding `bancoDeSolucoesPedagogicas` within `src/data/initialCases.ts`. My task now is to ensure it comprehensively addresses the nine neurodiverg\303\252ncias. I\'m actively working on incorporating these specifics, so I can start to provide better recommendations.\n\n\n**Incorporating Neurodiverg\303\252ncias Thoroughly**\n\nI\'m now integrating the additional neurodivergences \342\200\223 including anxiety disorders, learning disabilities, intellectual disabilities, OCD, mixed anxiety-depressive disorder, depressive disorders, and epilepsy \342\200\223 into the `bancoDeSolucoesPedagogicas`. I\'m working to expand the database with sensorial/physical considerations: visual impairments, motor difficulties, hearing impairments, and cases where there\'s no closed diagnosis, guided by MEC regulations. I\'m focusing on defining course profiles by considering the curriculum and course plan of a selected discipline in the attached file and how to translate that to `AddStudentModal.tsx`, in the Edit Component.\n\n\n**Defining Course Profiles**\n\nI\'ve shifted my focus to adding preset course profiles to the system, starting with Bachelor\'s in Information Systems and the Integrated High School Technical Course in Informatics. I\'m prioritizing the main subjects and professors that are already set in the attached file, for example, \"Engenharia de Software II\", \"Banco de Dados I / II\" and \"Algoritmos e L\303\263gica de Programa\303\247\303\243o\". I\'m also now planning to integrate the neurodivergences selection in the UI.\n\n\n**Developing UI Neurodivergence Interactions**\n\nI\'m now integrating the UI components to facilitate neurodivergence selection. My current focus is on creating interactive elements: clean buttons representing each neurodivergence, badges to indicate the academic level, and concise descriptions of the associated barriers in IT/Lab environments. When a user selects a neurodivergence, I\'m setting it to automatically load contextualized information: barriers specific to IT labs and disciplines, cognitive strengths, and relevant assistive technologies and DUA 3.0 accommodations.\n\n\n"
