  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Solution Display**\n\nI\'m now focusing on lines 836-860, specifically how `filteredSolutions` is presented. The goal is to customize this display based on a user\'s neurodivergence preferences (like ADHD). Instead of the current generic list, I\'m working to make the list more specific and relevant to the selected neurodivergence.\n\n\n**Listing Neurodivergences Now**\n\nI\'m structuring the display to prominently feature the nine neurodivergences as options for customization. I\'m building an array containing each condition\'s ID, name, acronym, and focus. This will guide Step 3, ensuring all nine conditions are selectable to personalize the learning experience.\n\n\n**Expanding Neurodivergence Options**\n\nI\'ve added specific details for anxiety disorders, learning disabilities (like dyslexia/dysgraphia), intellectual disabilities, and OCD to the neurodivergence array. I\'m focusing on tailoring the learning experience for each, including video substitutions, extended time allowances, open-source fonts, CI/CD pipelines, and explicit acceptance criteria to better support these conditions.\n\n\n**Adding New Neurodivergences**\n\nI\'ve incorporated three additional neurodivergences into the array: mixed anxiety-depressive disorder, depressive disorders, and epilepsy/seizure disorders. For each, I\'ve outlined specific pedagogical solutions. These include graduated goals and support channels for mixed disorders, asynchronous access and peer support for depression, and visual accommodations and safety protocols for epilepsy.\n\n\n**Connecting Courses, Subjects**\n\nI\'m now integrating course and subject connections. Based on course specifics like \"Bacharelado em Sistemas de Informa\303\247\303\243o\" (BSI) and \"Engenharia de Software II\" (BAC.0406), I\'m identifying related topics like software quality, TDD with JUnit/Selenium, and Jira bug tracking. I\'m also including assistive technology suggestions, such as Jira, Pomodoro, VS Code linters, and accommodations for conditions like low vision and motor difficulties.\n\n\n"
