  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Neurodivergencies**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got the basic structure for the `AddStudentModal.tsx` component sketched out. I\'m focusing now on defining the official neurodivergencies. I\'ve started by creating a constant array, `NEURODIVERGENCIAS_OFICIAIS`, and will populate it with the required data, like IDs.\n\n\n**Populating Neurodivergencies**\n\nI\'m currently populating the `NEURODIVERGENCIAS_OFICIAIS` array. I\'ve included several entries: TDAH, TEA, anxiety disorders, and specific learning disorders. Each entry includes an ID, name, acronym, icon, and a short summary highlighting accommodations for individuals with those specific neurodivergencies. I\'m focusing on accommodations directly relevant to the student\'s workflow.\n\n\n**Expanding Neurodivergencies**\n\nI\'ve added new entries to `NEURODIVERGENCIAS_OFICIAIS`, including intellectual disability/developmental disorder, OCD, mixed anxiety/depressive disorder, and depressive disorders. Each includes an ID, name, acronym, icon, and tailored accommodations. For instance, I\'ve outlined accommodations like step-by-step instructions for intellectual disability and explicit acceptance criteria for OCD.\n\n\n**Adding Accommodations**\n\nI\'ve just added epilepsy and seizure disorders to the list, detailing accommodations like stable refresh rate monitors, no-flash IDE themes, scheduled breaks, and safety protocols. I\'m also starting on course presets for Step 2. These presets will include label, course name, module, professor, and profile.\n\n\n**Listing Course Presets**\n\nI\'ve just added course presets to include label, course, discipline, module, professor, and profile. I\'ve populated this with Algoritmos e L\303\263gica de Programa\303\247\303\243o for BSI 1st period, Programa\303\247\303\243o Web e Algoritmos for the 2nd year of the Technical course, and Fundamentos de Redes e Hardware for the 1st year of the same Technical course. I\'m focusing on providing options directly relevant to the student\'s program.\n\n\n**Connecting Course Presets**\n\nNow, I\'m working to connect the course presets with automatic settings for `curso`, `disciplina`, `modulo`, `docenteRegente`, and `perfilModalidade`. This is directly linked to the PPC and Plano de Ensino information from the user\'s input. The goal is to streamline the student\'s workflow, making it easier to select the appropriate preset. I\'m focusing on the integration of these presets.\n\n\n**Integrating Jira Workflow**\n\nI\'m now integrating the Jira workflow into the system. This focuses on providing relevant support for project management and task tracking for the user\'s specific neurodivergency. I\'m aiming to offer the best project management experience.\n\n\n"
