    thinking: "**Analyzing Neurodivergence Data**\n\nOkay, I\'m currently focused on incorporating a new state variable, `categoriaNeurodivergencia`, into `AddStudentModal.tsx`, initializing it to \"Transtorno do D\303\251ficit de Aten\303\247\303\243o com Hiperatividade (TDAH)\". I also need to figure out how to handle the `mostrarOutros` logic, which will probably involve a conditional rendering element. The goal is to provide a user-friendly interface for capturing this specific student data.\n\n\n**Refining Condition Handling**\n\nI\'m now integrating detailed conditional data based on the `superior_ti` profile selection within the `handleSelectProfile` function. I\'m dynamically populating student data, specifically tailoring fields like `curso`, `modulo`, `disciplina`, `docenteRegente`, `idade`, `solucaoId`, `condicao`, `assistiveTech`, and `potencialidades` to reflect the specific neurodivergent conditions associated with the chosen profile. My focus is ensuring accurate and relevant data capture.\n\n\n**Implementing Neurodivergence Options**\n\nI\'ve just expanded the `handleSelectNeurodivergencia` function. It now takes IDs from the nine neurodivergence categories to update `categoriaNeurodivergencia`, `condicao`, `assistiveTech`, `potencialidades`, and `solucaoId`. Next, I\'m integrating interactive preset chips from the PPC do BSI and Plano de Ensino, which instantly populate course, discipline, module, and teacher fields upon selection. Finally, I\'m working on rendering the header, including the Portaria MEC status, and displaying the nine neurodivergences section.\n\n\n**Defining Neurodivergence Categories**\n\nI\'m currently structuring a section presenting nine neurodivergence options: Autism Spectrum Disorder (ASD), Anxiety Disorders, Specific Learning Disorder, Intellectual Disability, Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder (OCD), Mixed Anxiety and Depressive Disorder, Depressive Disorders, and Epilepsy. Each will highlight when selected, using a checkmark 