  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Neurodivergence Selection**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how best to allow for the multi-selection of neurodivergences in Step 3. The current design restricts selection to a single option, which doesn\'t reflect the common co-occurrence of conditions like autism and ADHD. I\'m exploring different UI approaches to enable multiple choices within this section to provide a more accurate and comprehensive representation.\n\n\n**Implementing Multi-Select Options**\n\nI\'ve been working on allowing users to select multiple neurodivergences. I\'m leaning towards checkboxes or toggle switches for the neurodivergence options to facilitate multi-selection in Step 3, which is a major update to the design. The generated PEI (both client-side and server-side) will need adapting to incorporate the combined challenges and strategies of all the chosen neurodivergences.\n\n**Adding Delete Confirmation**\n\nI\'m now focused on adding a PEI deletion feature. There will be an option to delete a PEI, likely in the PEI list/card view. When a user tries to delete a PEI, a confirmation modal will pop up. It will ask for confirmation, with a message like \"Are you sure you want to delete PEI N[ID] for [Student Name]?\" offering options to cancel or confirm deletion.\n\n\n"
