  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Conditional Logic**\n\nI\'ve been examining the conditional logic in `server.ts`, specifically lines 126-140. The current implementation uses a ternary chain that doesn\'t account for students with multiple diagnoses. It only evaluates the first true condition. My current thought is to revise this approach to correctly handle multiple conditions by implementing a new solution.\n\n\n**Refining Multi-Selection Strategy**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing multi-selection for neurodivergences in `AddStudentModal.tsx`. The shift is from a single `solucaoId` string to a `selectedSolucoes: string[]` array. This should allow multiple conditions like autism and ADHD to be selected. The UX needs toggling, and I need to add an exclusion option with a confirmation prompt for PEIs. I also need to make the PEI adapt to all selected neurodivergences.\n\n\n**Implementing Multi-Select Details**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the user interface for multi-selection. I\'m thinking of using checkboxes or interactive chips/cards to enable multiple selections. The UI needs to display the number of selected conditions and dynamically generate text combining all selected neurodivergences. This combined text will be used for different fields, including neurodivergence category, condition details, assistive technology, and potential cognitive strengths. The plan is to send an array of selected neurodivergences to the backend along with the barriers for the generation. Finally, I will also need to update `server.ts` to accept the new `selectedNeurodivergences` parameter in the request.\n\n\n**Enhancing Condition Handling**\n\nI\'m now revising the logic within `synthesizeIodaPei`. The goal is to move away from mutually exclusive checks and instead assess each neurodivergence individually. This involves iterating through each condition (`isAdhd`, etc.) and dynamically including strategies for Engajamento, Representa\303\247\303\243o, A\303\247\303\243o/Express\303\243o, and Avalia\303\247\303\243o based on *every* active condition. The smart goals (`metas`) will now incorporate objectives specific to *each* selected neurodivergence. I\'m also updating the Gemini prompt to explicitly mention co-occurring neurodivergences for comprehensive PEI generation.\n\n\n**Adding Delete Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating PEI deletion, focusing on where the user can delete a PEI. I\'m adding a card/list view in `ILovePeiHub.tsx` to list and manage PEIs, with options to view or delete. In `StudentHeader.tsx`, I\'ll include a delete button when viewing a student\'s PEI. Within `PeiView.tsx` and `OfficialTemplateView.tsx`, I\'m adding a delete button in the document header. Finally, I\'m making a reusable confirmation modal (`ConfirmDeleteModal.tsx`) to confirm deletion, with the title \"Confirma Exclus\303\243o?\".\n\n\n"
