  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing Lists in Server**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how to build additive lists within `server.ts`. I\'m starting by constructing lists for \'engajamento\', \'representacao\', \'acaoExpressao\', and \'taList\'. For example, I\'m thinking of how to push elements, such as \'Metodologia \303\241gil com ciclos curtos\', into the \'engajamentoList\' array when a condition like `isEngSoft` is met.\n\n\n**Refining Engagement Strategies**\n\nI\'ve been refining the engagement strategies, focusing on how different conditions influence the `engajamentoList`. Now, I\'m incorporating specific strategies for active neurodivergence, such as ADHD, Autism, and Anxiety. This involves adding elements to the list based on flags like `isAdhd` and `isAutism`, enriching the practical application for students with diverse needs.\n\n\n**Expanding Engagement Tactics**\n\nI\'m now expanding the engagement tactics to accommodate additional conditions. My focus is on how to integrate specific elements into the `engajamentoList` based on flags like `isOCD`, `isDepression`, `isEpilepsy`, `isLearning`, and `isIntellectual`, along with `isMotor`. I\'m aiming to create tailored engagement strategies to create an ideal experience for different needs.\n\n\n**Integrating Multiple Neurodivergences**\n\nI\'m now integrating the ability to select multiple neurodivergences, addressing cases where individuals present with overlapping conditions like TEA and TDAH. I\'m focusing on dynamically adapting the PEI (Individualized Educational Program) based on these selections. I\'m expanding this additive merging for `representacao`, `acaoExpressao`, `taList`, `barreiras`, and `objetivos_e_metas`. For example, if both TEA and TDAH are selected, the goals will merge new meta information into `objetivos_e_metas`.\n\n\n"
