  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Clarifying User Prompt**\n\nI\'ve been reviewing the code and decided to explicitly incorporate `neurodivergenciasSelecionadas` into the user prompt. Specifically, lines 454-463 informed this. I\'ll include a clear statement: \"Neurodiverg\303\252ncias Selecionadas (Comorbidade/M\303\272ltiplas): ${selectedNeurodivergences.join(\', \')}. ATEN\303\207\303\203O: O estudante apresenta mais de uma neurodiverg\303\252ncia.\" This should enhance clarity for the model.\n\n\n**Designing Delete Flow**\n\nI\'m now detailing the delete flow for PEIs. I\'m adding `peiToDelete`, `deleteSuccessNotice`, functions `handleRequestDeletePei`, `handleConfirmDeletePei`, and `handleCancelDelete` to `App.tsx`. The delete action will extract the student code and name, remove the PEI from `studentsList`, and update the active PEI. Success notices and modal management are also being implemented.\n\n\n**Implementing Delete UI**\n\nI\'m focusing on the user interface for PEI deletion. I\'m adding \"Excluir PEI\" buttons with trash icons across `Header.tsx`, `ILovePeiHub.tsx`, `PeiView.tsx`, and `OfficialTemplateView.tsx`. A confirmation modal will be created at `src/components/ConfirmDeleteModal.tsx`, featuring a warning icon and a clear question: \"Tem Certeza que quer excluir o PEI N#### do Aluno selecionado?\". This will improve the flow.\n\n\n**Refining Delete Confirmation**\n\nI\'m solidifying the delete confirmation modal. The question is now: \"Tem certeza que deseja excluir o PEI N\302\272 ${codigo} do estudante ${nome}?\". The context will display the course, component, matriculation/code, and a warning that data associated with the PEI will be removed. The \"Cancelar\" button will be emphasized for safety, and the \"Sim, Excluir PEI\" button will be visually distinct with a red background. I\'m taking the opportunity to refine Tailwind styling in `ConfirmDeleteModal.tsx`.\nI\'ll also review the multi-selection component in `AddStudentModal.tsx` as a reference.\n\n\n**Updating Solution Selection**\n\nI\'m refactoring the neurodivergence selection logic. Instead of a single `solucaoId`, I\'m moving to an array `selectedSolucoes`. This will enable multi-selection, controlled by a `handleToggleNeurodivergence` function. This function will add or remove solution IDs from the `selectedSolucoes` state, and handle the edge case of allowing deselecting all solutions. I\'m also preparing to fetch corresponding pedagogical solutions to update the UI accordingly.\n\n\n**Composing Output Data**\n\nI\'m now generating specific output data. I\'m focusing on crafting `condicao`, `assistiveTech`, and `potentialidades` fields. For `condicao`, I\'ll combine the descriptions and problems of selected objects, with contextualization for Engineering Software. `assistiveTech` will merge and deduplicate suggested resources. Finally, `potentialidades` will combine the unique potential of each selected condition.\n\n\n**Generating Potential Fields**\n\nI\'m now focusing on synthesizing the data for the `potentialidades` field. I\'m combining descriptions from solutions like `sol-ansiedade`, `sol-aprendizagem`, `sol-def-intelectual`, `sol-toc`, `sol-misto-ansioso-depressivo`, `sol-depressao`, and `sol-epilepsia` to create a consolidated and relevant output. I\'m using \"e\", when appropriate, to join matching entries and streamline the presentation.\n\n\n**Visualizing Step 3**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how neurodivergences will be visually displayed in Step 3 of `AddStudentModal.tsx`. I\'ve added a checkmark on each card. When selected, the card will display a green highlight. Above the grid will be an alert badge explaining multiple selection is activated, a selected tags counter with individual \"\303\227\" to remove items, and a quick \"Desmarcar todas\" action.\n\n\n"
