  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Requirements**\n\nI\'m meticulously dissecting the user\'s requirements, focusing intently on the initial request regarding the `AddStudentModal`. My aim is a comprehensive and precise refactoring, ensuring every aspect is addressed with clarity and accuracy. I\'m focusing on dissecting the initial requirement now.\n\n\n**Refining Interface Design**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the \"Neurodivergence Selection\" component. The current clutter is the key problem. My solution involves a streamlined \"Chip / Checkbox\" interface, displaying only the condition name and a checkbox. The detailed descriptions will be hidden, available via a \"View Summary\" button. Furthermore, I\'ll be adding a \"Dictate by Voice\" feature to the observation fields within the `AddStudentModal.tsx` in Stage 3.\n\n\n**Streamlining Interface Clutter**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a complete interface declutter, specifically targeting redundant elements. My immediate goal is to compact the student header for a cleaner presentation and eliminate duplicated navigation bars in `App.tsx`. I\'ll also be removing the distracting \"Art. 11\" and legal citations from the main screens, moving them to the footer.\n\n\n**Refining Document Layout**\n\nI\'m now overhauling the layout of `PeiView.tsx` to increase whitespace, reduce clashing borders (especially the colored boxes), and organize sections into clean, concise blocks, emphasizing essential information. I\'m also simplifying navigation labels in `Navbar.tsx` and `ILovePeiHub.tsx`, opting for direct names with accompanying icons, like \"In\303\255cio\", \"Plano de Aula (PEI)\", \"Estudo de Caso\", \"Metas e Notas\", and \"Imprimir p/ SEI\". I\'m also working to improve the pedagogical strategy generator, aiming for more elaborate and practical suggestions.\n\n\n**Developing Practical Classroom Guide**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in developing the \"Practical Classroom Guide,\" focusing on its structure and content. I\'m structuring a practical, step-by-step guide for classroom use, which includes concrete steps for explaining subject matter, breaking down tasks, creating assessment criteria, and managing student challenges. I\'m adding an optional `guiaPraticoSalaDeAula` field to `SolucaoCondicao` and `PlanejamentoPEI` for pedagogical solutions, making sure there is 100% type compatibility in `pei.ts` and integrating it with `bancoDeSolucoesPedagogicas`. I\'ll integrate it with the generator (`server.ts`, `gerarNovoPeiCompleto`) and neatly display it in `PeiView.tsx` and `SolutionBankModal.tsx`. Also I will add a \"View Student Guide\" button within `PeiView.tsx` so students can see their goals as a checklist.\n\n\n**Implementing Voice Dictation**\n\nI\'m now implementing voice dictation using the Web Speech API. I\'m focusing on creating reusable components for the \"Dictate by Voice\" and \"Listen\" buttons in Portuguese. I\'m building features for speech recognition in the observation fields and text-to-speech for strategies within the PEI, incorporating visual feedback for the user experience.\n\n\n\n"
