    checkpoint_index: 7
    session_summary: "<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - **Current User Request**: The user asked (in Portuguese): *\"na parte de imprimir/salvar pdf o botao nao faz nada isso \303\251 pq estou so numa preview ou \303\251 algum erro?\"* (\"In the print/save PDF part, the button does nothing\342\200\224is this because I\'m just in a preview or is it an error?\").\n   - **Goal**:\n     1. Explain clearly why `window.print()` is blocked/ignored inside the sandboxed AI Studio preview `<iframe>` (or inspect how the button is currently implemented in `/src/components/` or `/src/App.tsx`).\n     2. Improve the implementation so that the user can actually export/download a PDF or print reliably inside the preview environment (e.g., generating a direct `.pdf` file download via `jspdf` / `html2pdf.js` or a clean client-side PDF generator, in addition to or replacing a blocked `window.print()`), so the button works immediately inside the preview iframe as well as in a full browser tab.\n   - **Environment URLs**:\n     - Development App URL: `https://ais-dev-krwzzynhegkqukx43cumqj-729395395096.us-west2.run.app`\n     - Shared App URL: `https://ais-pre-krwzzynhegkqukx43cumqj-729395395096.us-west2.run.app`\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - **Completed Previously**:\n     - Fixed the Vite 8 host-check block (`403 Forbidden` on `*.run.app`) and ESM `__dirname` issues in `/vite.config.ts` and `/server.ts`, plus cleaned up `/tsconfig.json`.\n     - Verified with `lint_applet`, `compile_applet`, `restart_dev_server`, and `curl -i -s -H \"Host: ais-dev-krwzzynhegkqukx43cumqj-729395395096.us-west2.run.app\" http://localhost:3000/` (returned `HTTP/1.1 200 OK`).\n   - **In Progress (Current Turn)**:\n     - Listed `/src` contents:\n       - `/src/App.tsx`\n       - `/src/components` (directory)\n       - `/src/data` (directory)\n       - `/src/index.css`\n       - `/src/main.tsx`\n       - `/src/types` (directory)\n     - Have not yet inspected `/src/components` or `/src/App.tsx` to see the exact \"Imprimir / Salvar PDF\" button implementation.\n\n3. **Key Findings**\n   - In the AI Studio preview environment, the app runs inside a cross-origin sandboxed `<iframe>`. Calling `window.print()` inside a sandboxed iframe without `allow-modals` is silently blocked by browsers (or ignored), which makes a button calling `window.print()` appear to do nothing in the preview.\n   - Additionally, `/src` does not have a `/src/pages` directory; components live in `/src/components` and `/src/App.tsx`.\n\n4. **Errors & Fixes**\n   - **Resolved**: Vite 8 blocked requests from `ais-dev-*.run.app` with `403 Forbidden` because `server.allowedHosts: true` was missing in `vite.config.ts`. Fixed by adding `allowedHosts: true` to `vite.config.ts` and `server.ts`.\n   - **Tool Error**: Attempted `view_file` on `/src/pages/ReportPage.tsx`, which failed because `/src/pages` does not exist. Immediately ran `list_dir` on `/src` and found `/src/components` and `/src/App.tsx`.\n\n5. **Active Context**\n   - Dev server is running cleanly on port 3000 (`server.ts` with Express + Vite middleware).\n   - No background tasks are pending.\n\n6. **Next Steps**\n   1. List `/src/components` (using `list_dir`) and inspect `/src/App.tsx` and the report/PDF component (using `view_file`) to see how the \"Imprimir / Salvar PDF\" button is currently wired.\n   2. Implement a real, direct PDF download (e.g., using `jspdf` or `html2canvas`/`jspdf` if needed, or check `package.json` first via `view_file` to see what packages are already installed) or provide a direct PDF download action alongside `window.print()` so clicking the button works seamlessly inside the preview iframe without relying on `window.print()` / `window.open()`.\n   3. Run `lint_applet` and `compile_applet` if any code changes are made.\n   4. Answer the user\'s question in Portuguese clearly: explain that `window.print()` is blocked by browser security inside the preview iframe, and confirm that the button now generates/downloads the PDF directly so it works inside the preview as well.\n\n7. **Commitments & Constraints**\n   - Communicate in Portuguese (matching the user\'s language).\n   - Follow environment constraints: avoid `window.alert` / `window.open` as primary flows since the app runs in an iframe; keep the UI clean and functional.\n</summary>"
