  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Print Functionality**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `handlePrint` function in `/src/App.tsx`. The core logic focuses on ensuring the \'documento_oficial\' tab is active before triggering the print command. A `setTimeout` is used, presumably to allow for any necessary state updates or rendering before `window.print()` is called. I\'m exploring the implications of this delay, and what dependencies the printing process has on the active tab\'s content.\n\n\n"
